ent address 10.100.122.10:80 that round-robins to backend HTTP servers on node2 and node3 (Python http.server on port 8080, each identifying its own hostname/IP). Verified node4 receives alternating responses from both backends through this single entry point, both before and after sequentially restarting all four nodes with independent boot-identity proof and post-restart recovery verification.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Surveyed all 4 nodes: node1 is OPNsense (FreeBSD/pf) with a single LAN interface 10.100.122.10/24 shared with node2/node3/node4 (Ubuntu 24.04)\",\"Installed a simple-http systemd service on node2 and node3 serving distinct hostname-identifying content on TCP 8080\",\"Verified node1 could reach both backends over 8080 before touching HAProxy\",\"Installed the os-haproxy plugin via pkg on node1\",\"Edited /conf/config.xml (with backup) to add two HAProxy servers (node2, node3 on 8080), one roundrobin backend pool, and one frontend bound to 10.100.122.10:80 forwarding to the pool\",\"Reloaded the HAProxy template, ran configtest (haproxy -c), confirmed the generated config, and started the haproxy service\",\"Confirmed the existing pf pass rule for tcp/80 to self already permitted the new listener without weakening SSH management access\",\"Verified round-robin load balancing from node4 through node1:80 alternating between node2 and node3 responses\",\"Captured baseline boot identity (kern.boottime for FreeBSD node1, boot_id for Linux nodes 2-4) and service health for all nodes\",\"Sequentially restarted node1, node2, node3, node4 one at a time using native reboot mechanisms (shutdown -r / reboot), polling until each came back\",\"Proved changed boot identity for each node post-restart and verified HAProxy (node1), backend HTTP services (node2/node3), and end-to-end load-balanced access from node4 all recovered\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node2 and node3 each serve HTTP on 8080 identifying which host answered\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d520becd01c04bbb\",\"cmd-6a8bb823c9bb463d\"],\"summary\":\"Installed and started simple-http systemd service on node2 and node3; curl localhost:8080 on each returns 'Hello from node2 (10.100.122.11)' and 'Hello from node3 (10.100.122.12)' respectively\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 reaches both backends over the shared private network prior to LB config\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d0b8cc34993e47cc\"],\"summary\":\"fetch from node1 to http://10.100.122.11:8080 and http://10.100.122.12:8080 both succeed and return the distinct hostname content\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 presents one entry point on TCP 80 of its management address that spreads requests across both hosts\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e2f14d1fec2246df\",\"cmd-7a17629c71f04e2b\",\"cmd-17a227070fee4b13\",\"cmd-4c43d56556904f10\"],\"summary\":\"config.xml edited to add HAProxy servers/backend/frontend, template reload rendered a valid haproxy.conf with frontend bind 10.100.122.10:80 balancing roundrobin across node2/node3:8080, config passed haproxy -c syntax check, and haproxy started listening on 10.100.122.10:80 (sockstat confirms)\"},{\"requirement\":\"firewall does not block the new entry point / SSH management path preserved\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7ae1410562e547e9\"],\"summary\":\"pfctl -s rules shows a pre-existing pass rule for tcp/http (port 80) to self on vtnet0, plus the untouched ssh pass rule, so no risky filter reload was needed\"},{\"requirement\":\"node4 receives answers from each of node2 and node3 through node1's entry point\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-cf5ea1eb400d44cc\"],\"summary\":\"8 sequential curls from node4 to http://10.100.122.10:80/ alternate perfectly between 'Hello from node2' and 'Hello from node3'\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-27ca02eb2fae496b\",\"cmd-9be4efcc5a79404e\",\"cmd-31cea92272da478b\",\"cmd-87dd671166594aea\",\"cmd-76a4fffb03134e8d\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline kern.boottime=1788630765 (17:52: